From a0b11e16b48026d7bff624448714c4178e649da0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:29:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: each machine's camera gets its own seat's events

The game has 9 cameras (0x80601D28 + n x 0x25C) and sends a racer's events
(jumps, tricks, boosts, dash panels) to the camera of its index (+0x1029).
View 0 shows camera 0, which followed this machine's seat, but racer 0's
events still went to it: on Knuckles's screen the camera took Sonic's jump
angle and effects (Gibax, 6"00 on Metal City).

The 258 reads of the index that only address a camera now read +0x106C during
the race, a racer byte the game never uses, written each frame: camera 0 for
this machine's seat, camera 1 for a second seat, the seat's own camera for the
racer that had them. Every racer keeps a camera of its own. +0x106C is left out
of the checksum. SRNP_CAMERAS=0 keeps the game's reads.

Also: the effect drawn from the player's camera at 0x8054E644 reads the
shifted index, and the index caves use addic for r0.

Measured in the 2-player race (both AI-driven): Knuckles's camera at 6"00 is
behind him again; his own trick camera on the big jump is unchanged; 31
identical checksums, 0 divergences.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
