                on ? "camera 0's, from racer 0's path only" : "the game's");
 }
 
+// The cameras (2026-11-26, Gibax: "la cam de knuckles a 6"00 ... copie l'angle et l'effet de celle
+// de Sonic"). The game has 9 cameras (0x80601D28 + n x 0x25C) and a racer's events (jumps, tricks,
+// boosts, dash panels...) go to the camera of its index (+0x1029): these 258 reads of the index serve
+// only to address a camera (x 0x25C, at most a test < 9 before), found in the REL's code (lbz rD,
+// 0x1029(rA) whose register goes nowhere else). View 0 shows camera 0, which follows this machine's
+// seat (kCameraRacer), but racer 0's events still went to it. During the race these reads take
+// +0x106C instead, a byte no code of the game uses (zero in every racer through whole races, dumps of
+// 2026-11-25), written each frame: the camera of each racer's events, camera 0 for this machine's
+// seat (camera 1 for its second seat) and the seat's own for the racer that had camera 0. Every racer
+// keeps a camera of its own; only which one is shown differs between machines. The read at 0x80574608
+// (kIndexReads) already sends the seat's racer to camera 0. SRNP_CAMERAS=0 keeps the game's.
